comments.body:
> @senthil-nexthop The wait_for_stat_stable() change looks like a good fix for the stats publish race, but the new pushed >= 1 assertions in the MAC ping-pong and bulk-learn tests feel too relaxed compared to the original expectations. Since these tests are primarily validating FDB churn behavior, could we keep a conservative lower bound that still reflects the burst being exercised, while relying on STATE_DB for the exact functional check?

@prabhataravind thanks for the review. There are couple of reasons why the check on `pushed` stats was relaxed. There are some ASIC platforms which could suppress rapid MOVEs at the ASIC layer. And there are SAI adapters that batch multiple notifications into a single PUBLISH event. So a 50 cycles generating 100 notifications could be batched into 3 PUBLISH calls, each with multiple notifications. This is seen and reported on some Cisco platforms.

So the `pushed >= cycles` check is not portable and instead of checking for a really low bar (of 1), I've raised the floor to  `min_pushed` that accounts for both types of platforms mentioned above.
